Always verify the user before a saved password is filled on OHOS.

The product dropped the "verify before filling" switch: every fill asks,
as viewing, copying, editing and exporting already did.
IsReauthBeforeFillingRequired no longer reads
ohos.password_fill_requires_auth. A phone with nothing enrolled still
fills, as before: there is nothing to ask with.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-password-fill-always-auth.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc b/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
index 993577f..5574e16 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/password_manager/chrome_password_manager_client.cc
@@ -762,14 +762,14 @@ bool ChromePasswordManagerClient::IsReauthBeforeFillingRequired(
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
   // The desktop answer goes through PasswordFeatureManager, which reads
   // a local-state pref written by a Views promo bubble this platform
-  // does not have. Read the setting the shell owns instead.
+  // does not have. Here it is not a setting at all: the product asks
+  // every fill to be verified, and the shell no longer offers a switch
+  // (ohos.password_fill_requires_auth is no longer read).
   //
-  // Off by the user's choice is honoured; off because nothing is
-  // enrolled is not a choice, but there is nothing to ask with either,
-  // so filling goes ahead. What is behind the lock in that case is the
-  // store itself, which HUKS holds.
-  return authenticator && GetPrefs() &&
-         GetPrefs()->GetBoolean("ohos.password_fill_requires_auth") &&
+  // A phone with nothing enrolled has nothing to ask with, so filling
+  // goes ahead; what is behind the lock in that case is the store itself,
+  // which HUKS holds.
+  return authenticator &&
          authenticator->CanAuthenticateWithBiometricOrScreenLock();
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
     BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
